Revision history for Email-Barcode-Decode

0.05   not released yet
    - replaced Image::Magick with Imager; ImageMagick 6.9.11 (Debian 12)
      returned empty YUV blobs, which made Barcode::ZBar segfault
    - die with "raster size mismatch" instead of passing a short raster to
      Barcode::ZBar
    - enhancers simplified to plain grayscale and a black/white threshold;
      they now get an Imager object and return ($raw, 'Y800', $width, $height)
    - PDF pages are rendered with `pdftoppm -gray` (poppler-utils) instead of
      Ghostscript: lossless grayscale instead of JPEG, PDF-only parser
      instead of a PostScript interpreter
    - attached_files of PDF pages are now named <name>-pdf-page-N.pgm
      (was <name>-pdf-pageN.jpg); page numbers are zero-padded, which fixes
      the page order of PDFs with 10 or more pages

0.04   21 September 2016
    - fixes to still work after debian/jessie
      libmagickwand-6.q16-2 libmagickcore-6.q16-2 imagemagick-common packages
      security update to 8:6.8.9.9-5+deb8u4

0.03   18 March 2016
    - improved B/W enhacing of image to be decoded

0.02    4 Feb 2016
    - scaling down images to 1500px, bigger images may not work well with Barcode::ZBar::Image
    - normalize and sharpen contrast before decoding

0.01    4 Jan 2013
        First version, released on an unsuspecting world.

